        "text": "Security update for curl",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for curl fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-5773: wrong reuse of SMB connection (bsc#1262633).\n- CVE-2026-7168: cross-proxy Digest auth state leak (bsc#1263440).\n- CVE-2026-8926: password leak with netrc and user in URL (bsc#1268412).\n- CVE-2026-13608: OpenLDAP SASL authentication bypass (bsc#1277476).\n- CVE-2026-80229: OpenSSL provider use-after-free (bsc#1277479).\n- CVE-2026-80230: OpenSSL pinning bypass (bsc#1277480).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
